WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.420
In Search of Dharma.

2
00:00:05.064 --> 00:00:05.960
9: Coda.

3
00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:12.680
Eight parts of searching have earned one
plain definition and two tests.

4
00:00:13.511 --> 00:00:16.200
So here they are, stated rather than
argued:

5
00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.020
what a dharma is, and how to tell the
better ones ...

6
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.300
A dharma is a way of living that tells a
person or group how to act,

7
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:30.120
what to value, what to avoid, and what
kind of life is worth trying to become.

8
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.340
A dharma is not necessarily a religion.

9
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:39.580
It is a living ethical orientation: a
pattern of values, habits, stories,

10
00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:44.580
duties, practices and social expectations
that helps humans navigate the world.

11
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.320
Most dharmas are inherited half-consciously
and never feel chosen at all;

12
00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.640
a few are examined, reformed, or built on
purpose.

13
00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:56.220
The word describes what a thing does, not
how well:

14
00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:00.180
gentle and cruel, living and hollowed, all
are dharmas.

15
00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:04.300
Whether one is any good is a separate
question, answered below.

16
00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:09.120
At its deepest level, a dharma is that
which holds a life,

17
00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.380
a community, or a world together.

18
00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:15.920
There is no single "the Dharma"

19
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.380
It is better to say a dharma than the
Dharma,

20
00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.880
because human beings create many dharmas.

21
00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.740
And the word itself is a placeholder.

22
00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:32.440
Every culture builds the thing and names
it in its own tongue: Ubuntu, ma'at,

23
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:37.860
and Tao are not translations of dharma but
sibling names for sibling instances.

24
00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:41.700
The Sanskrit is kept because, of all the
candidates,

25
00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:45.400
its root says most plainly what the thing
does: hold.

26
00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:51.820
A Buddhist dharma, a Hindu dharma, a
scientific-rationalist dharma,

27
00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.820
a warrior dharma, an environmental dharma,

28
00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:57.680
a professional dharma, a family dharma,

29
00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.500
a personal dharma: all of these are
candidates.

30
00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:03.420
But coherence alone does not make a
dharma.

31
00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:06.240
What marks one off from mere custom, law,

32
00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.680
or etiquette is a combination of four
features:

33
00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.080
Comprehensive -- it governs a whole life,

34
00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.760
or a whole domain of one, not a single
slice of behaviour.

35
00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.200
Identity-constituting -- it binds from the
inside,

36
00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:25.420
by conviction, and works to remake its
carrier.

37
00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:30.760
Oriented toward the good -- an answer to
how one ought to live,

38
00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:34.380
as its carriers conceive it, not a
strategy for getting ahead.

39
00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:39.800
Reflectively self-aware -- it can be held
up and known as a path:

40
00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:42.240
named, questioned, reformed.

41
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:47.940
The features come in degrees; a
profession, a subculture,

42
00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:52.360
an environmentalism may carry two or
three, and sit near the rim.

43
00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.420
Religious dharmas do not have automatic
privilege over secular ones.

44
00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.580
All dharmas can be studied as human
cultural systems

45
00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:05.240
for answering the same practical question:

46
00:03:07.059 --> 00:03:08.300
How should we live?

47
00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:12.540
What a dharma contains

48
00:03:15.513 --> 00:03:17.300
A dharma usually includes:

49
00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:20.800
Values -- what matters.

50
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.360
Ethics -- what is appropriate or
inappropriate.

51
00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.980
Practices -- what one repeatedly does.

52
00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:34.140
Stories -- why life is this way.

53
00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:40.560
Duties -- what one owes to self, others,
community, or world.

54
00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:46.580
Community -- whom one belongs to, and who
holds one to the path.

55
00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:52.740
Identity -- who "we" are, or who "I" am
trying to become.

56
00:03:54.660 --> 00:04:00.620
Discipline -- how one trains conduct,
attention, speech, desire, and response.

57
00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:09.200
Transmission -- how the way is handed on:
by story, example, drill, and correction.

58
00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:15.460
A dharma is more than an idea: it becomes
real through behaviour.

59
00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:20.620
It is embodied in how one speaks, works,
eats, raises children,

60
00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:25.820
handles conflict, treats strangers,
responds to suffering, and uses power.

61
00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.520
Why humans need dharmas

62
00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:37.280
Humans are cooperative primates with
dangerous capacities: love and cruelty,

63
00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:42.760
loyalty and tribal hatred, care and
domination, imagination and self-deception.

64
00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:46.940
A dharma helps regulate these forces.

65
00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:51.560
It gives structure to conduct, makes
people more predictable to one another,

66
00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:54.360
and helps groups coordinate, reduce
conflict,

67
00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.660
transmit wisdom, and preserve meaning
across generations.

68
00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:02.020
In this sense, a dharma is a kind of
ethical

69
00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:04.860
software running on human biological
hardware.

70
00:05:06.561 --> 00:05:08.800
It does not erase our animal nature.

71
00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.300
It trains it.

72
00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.960
And none of this survives on its own.

73
00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.380
Every carrier of a dharma dies,

74
00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:20.360
so a dharma persists only by reproducing
itself in new people:

75
00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:25.040
taught by story and example, grooved in by
practice and repetition,

76
00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:28.240
held in place by a community that notices
when it slips.

77
00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:31.400
Call it education, in the broadest sense,

78
00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:34.160
so long as the word is allowed to include
all of that;

79
00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.100
explicit instruction is the smallest part
of it,

80
00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:39.820
and most of the teaching happens below
argument,

81
00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:43.180
which is why a dharma feels inherited
rather than chosen.

82
00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:47.900
A dharma that cannot reproduce itself dies
with the people who hold it,

83
00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.360
however wise it was.

84
00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.200
And no dharma is built from nothing.

85
00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:58.000
New dharmas emerge from within the cultures
and communities that carry their makers,

86
00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:02.700
and they inherit the materials of those
cultures, the worse along with the better.

87
00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:06.540
The craft lies in choosing what deserves
to go on holding.

88
00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:11.380
How a dharma survives translation

89
00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:16.720
A dharma can be carried out of its old
cosmology,

90
00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:19.600
and the record holds both successes and
husks.

91
00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:24.040
The translations that keep their
transforming power do three things.

92
00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:26.760
They keep the whole bundle: practice,

93
00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:30.460
ethics and community together, never the
soothing technique alone.

94
00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:35.360
They put some this-worldly replacement in
the place the old metaphysics held:

95
00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:39.140
something that still binds, still
motivates, still endures.

96
00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:42.220
And they remain a way of life one
practises,

97
00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:44.400
rather than a worldview one merely holds.

98
00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:48.540
Do all three and a dharma can survive the
loss of its gods.

99
00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:52.060
Do only the first, and the result is a
product.

100
00:06:55.246 --> 00:06:56.200
The two tests

101
00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:03.180
Holding is not by itself goodness, and
plural is not the same as equal.

102
00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:05.780
A dharma is judged by two tests.

103
00:07:07.758 --> 00:07:11.880
The first is substantive: the better
dharmas hold without crushing.

104
00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:15.140
They gather a life or a community into
shape and meaning

105
00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:18.540
without breaking the people inside them or
the strangers outside them.

106
00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:22.140
A dharma that holds but crushes is a
tyranny;

107
00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:25.580
one that refuses to crush but cannot hold
is a mood.

108
00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:30.680
The second is procedural, and it is the
keystone:

109
00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:35.220
dharmas are better to the extent they remain
revisable by the people bound by them.

110
00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:40.220
Not revisable by guardians alone, and not
reformed from outside,

111
00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:44.020
however enlightened the outsiders:
revisable by the bound.

112
00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.580
Dharmas are made things,

113
00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:51.220
and an unrevisable dharma is a made thing
pretending to be found.

114
00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:54.400
The first test asks what a dharma does.

115
00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:57.660
The second asks who holds the pen.

116
00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:02.120
Not everything that holds deserves to keep
holding.

117
00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:04.480
These two tests are how to tell.

118
00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:08.980
A personal dharma

119
00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:15.540
A personal dharma is the way an individual
consciously chooses to live.

120
00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.800
But it is never made alone:

121
00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:21.600
even the most personal dharma is built
from inherited language,

122
00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:22.680
examples, communities,

123
00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.760
obligations and refusals, and it needs
company,

124
00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:30.420
and someone to answer to, if it is to be
more than a private mood.

125
00:08:32.722 --> 00:08:36.980
It is not necessarily a mystical destiny
or a fixed "life purpose."

126
00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:39.360
It is more like a cultivated path:

127
00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:43.020
a way of accepting reality, responding to
difficulty,

128
00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:44.900
reducing unnecessary harm,

129
00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:48.060
and leaving the place a little better held
than one found it.

130
00:08:49.752 --> 00:08:51.820
A mature personal dharma asks:

131
00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:55.860
What do I care about above all else?

132
00:08:57.820 --> 00:09:01.120
What kind of person do I become through my
repeated actions?

133
00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.160
What do my habits actually serve?

134
00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:10.140
Does my way of living reduce suffering or
increase it?

135
00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:14.560
Does it help only me, or does it help us?

136
00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:19.500
The question that dissolves

137
00:09:21.796 --> 00:09:22.860
For readers who came

138
00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:25.800
from the secular-dharma world carrying its
standing worry

139
00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:30.460
(is what we practise still Buddhism? is it
really a dharma?):

140
00:09:31.169 --> 00:09:35.460
the eight parts behind this page dissolve
the question rather than answer it.

141
00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:39.040
Dharmas are made, plural, and revisable.

142
00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:42.840
The living questions are the ones above:
what are we building,

143
00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:45.980
does it hold without crushing, and who
holds the pen?

144
00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:52.220
A dharma is a way of living that holds a
person or a people together.

145
00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:57.340
The better ones hold without crushing, and
leave the pen in the hands of those held.

